WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:03.524
"I need to get to Gem's Jewelry," Roxy thought.

2
00:00:03.525 --> 00:00:07.160
"I have to find out why things are disappearing."

3
00:00:07.161 --> 00:00:09.790
Mara was far ahead in the race by now.

4
00:00:09.791 --> 00:00:16.680
But Terrell and Jack were running slowly.

5
00:00:16.681 --> 00:00:22.736
"Hey . . . guys." Roxy pretended to breathe hard.

6
00:00:22.737 --> 00:00:28.747
"Whew! I'm out of breath. I—um, I need to walk for a—a bit."

7
00:00:28.748 --> 00:00:31.719
Jack slowed down. "Oh, good!"

8
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.798
He was still gasping for air.

9
00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:36.471
"I'll . . . walk with you."

10
00:00:36.472 --> 00:00:41.468
"Uh-oh," Roxy thought. "I can't leave if Jack is with me."

11
00:00:41.469 --> 00:00:43.528
Terrell gave Roxy a quick look.

12
00:00:43.529 --> 00:00:45.712
Then he started to run faster.

13
00:00:45.713 --> 00:00:48.572
"Hey, Jack!" he called over his shoulder.

14
00:00:48.573 --> 00:00:51.313
"I'm going to beat you!"

15
00:00:51.314 --> 00:00:54.122
"No way!" Jack cried.

16
00:00:54.123 --> 00:00:56.320
He hurried after Terrell.

17
00:00:56.321 --> 00:01:00.011
"Thanks, Terrell," Roxy thought.

18
00:01:00.012 --> 00:01:03.426
*** Seconds later Roxy arrived at Gem's

19
00:01:03.427 --> 00:01:05.680
Jewelry. Detective Smith was already

20
00:01:05.681 --> 00:01:08.878
there. Gem stood behind an empty jewelry

21
00:01:08.879 --> 00:01:12.106
case. "Hey, Detective!" Roxy

22
00:01:12.107 --> 00:01:17.543
smiled. "Are you here to buy something for your

23
00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:22.405
sweetheart?" Detective Smith turned red. "Actually, um . . .

24
00:01:22.406 --> 00:01:28.155
" Roxy gasped. "You are? I was just

25
00:01:28.156 --> 00:01:31.080
kidding." Detective Smith

26
00:01:31.081 --> 00:01:36.271
sighed. "Yes, Rocket Girl. I was here to buy a necklace for

27
00:01:36.272 --> 00:01:40.515
someone. But then all the jewelry in the store

28
00:01:40.516 --> 00:01:44.719
disappeared." Gem nodded. "It was so strange.

29
00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:49.244
One moment all of my jewelry cases were full.

30
00:01:49.245 --> 00:01:51.428
The next moment, poof!

31
00:01:51.429 --> 00:01:55.465
They were empty." She frowned.

32
00:01:55.466 --> 00:01:59.752
"I hope you can find my jewelry."

33
00:01:59.753 --> 00:02:03.057
"Did you see anything odd?" Roxy asked.

34
00:02:03.058 --> 00:02:07.176
"Did anything happen before the jewelry vanished?"

35
00:02:07.177 --> 00:02:09.154
Detective Smith nodded.

36
00:02:09.155 --> 00:02:11.891
"Something seemed to move through the store.

37
00:02:11.892 --> 00:02:15.663
But it was so fast. We couldn't see what it was."

38
00:02:15.664 --> 00:02:19.745
"It was like a strong wind blowing through here."

39
00:02:19.746 --> 00:02:23.932
Gem threw up her arms. "Whoosh!"

40
00:02:23.933 --> 00:02:25.787
Roxy rubbed her chin.

41
00:02:25.788 --> 00:02:30.155
"Mayor Bloom said people called about other things vanishing."

42
00:02:30.156 --> 00:02:33.023
"Yes," Detective Smith said.

43
00:02:33.024 --> 00:02:36.641
"And it all happened in the last ten minutes.

44
00:02:36.642 --> 00:02:40.404
The first call came from two Shopwell Supermarket workers.

45
00:02:40.405 --> 00:02:43.836
They were carrying money, but it disappeared."

46
00:02:43.837 --> 00:02:46.138
"Wow," Roxy said.

47
00:02:46.139 --> 00:02:50.219
"If these are robberies, the thief is really fast!"

48
00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.750
Detective Smith's phone beeped.

49
00:02:52.751 --> 00:02:58.470
"Hello? Oh no! Okay, we'll check it out." He looked at Roxy.

50
00:02:58.471 --> 00:03:00.960
"A clothing store up the street was just robbed."

51
00:03:00.961 --> 00:03:05.249
Fwoosh! A strong wind blew down the sidewalk outside.

52
00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.850
Papers fluttered through the air.

53
00:03:07.851 --> 00:03:12.081
Gem raised an eyebrow. "Do you think that was—"

54
00:03:12.082 --> 00:03:14.767
"The thief!" Roxy said.

55
00:03:14.768 --> 00:03:17.122
Detective Smith put his phone away.

56
00:03:17.123 --> 00:03:23.781
"Okay, Rocket Girl. We should . . . Rocket Girl?"

